      "writtenOn": "2024-11-18T23:04:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e How would someone create this object in a test?\n\nGood question to which I don\u0027t have the answer.  \nAre you suggesting I should provide an API constructor, even if that doesn\u0027t make sense to have one in a normal usage ? In this case, should this be a systemApi, or can I restrict this to \"testApi\" (I never did one of such) ?\n\nRight now, this object is only constructed as part of the return of `getAudioInputControlServices`, and the only test implemented are end-to-end test, where the real API are called to emulate valide user journey scenario.\nI have no test for API negative testing because of that yet.",
      "parentUuid": "ffa7a794_b71dc4b3",
      "revId": "c9439e9f79672fd4b07803accaba5f5d21290398",
