      "writtenOn": "2024-11-19T16:57:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, while CTS tests are valuable, if I\u0027m an app developer and I need to use these APIs in a test, it becomes a lot harder to do so if I can\u0027t create a version of this object.\n\nOne way to do this is to just have a constructor (it would need to also be @SystemApi or public API if there\u0027s public APIs that use this) and document that it is only visible for testing.\n\n@TestApi is meant for exposing things specifically for CTS tests, not for external testing.\n\nAlternatively, you can have a method that will return a real object, if that makes more sense (for instance, if you can\u0027t expose every parameter of the ctor).",
      "parentUuid": "fc2add23_d64a412c",
      "revId": "c9439e9f79672fd4b07803accaba5f5d21290398",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
