      "message": "I don\u0027t think you can mock a class if the ctor is private.\n\nA Fake for this would work instead, since it does seem infeasible to expose this class as is.\n\nUnfortunately, we\u0027re a bit stuck. Because right now, these APIs are not testable. Quoting from go/android-api-guidelines: \"APIs should also be testable. You should be able to answer the question, \"How will an app developer test code that uses your API?\"",
