      "side": 1,
      "message": "It would be a user friendly name of what this AICS is about. It is helpful when multiple AICS with the same type are on a device.  \nFor example if the input is DIGITAL, they could set it to \"HDMI\" / \"USB\" / ...\n\nCloser to the usecase of this release of API the audio input type \"Streaming\" could refer to telecoil or auracast, two concurrent technology. Since there is no AudioInputType to differentiate them, it would be up to the Description to do it.\n\nBut the value of the description is a free field that can be anything, and device could exposes capabilities to rename it by the end user.",
